The local backfill script ingests historical price data from 2023-01-01 to the current date. The code filters S&amp;P 500 by MIN_MARKET_CAP = 10_000_000_000, partitions prices by individual trading date, and writes a company info snapshot on the day the script runs.
The local backfill script does not write us_financials_raw.parquet. Financials are ingested via the daily ingestion pipeline; the transformation code includes appropriate fallback handlers.
Install Local Dependencies # Create a dedicated virtual environment for local backfill. python -m venv .venv .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1 # Install packages required by source imports. pip install boto3 pandas requests yfinance pyarrow tqdm lxml Preparation and Run Backfill Step Action Technical Details 1 Create file backfill_raw_ingestion.py Use the full source code below 2 Verify BUCKET_NAME Must be stock-screener-raw-your-name 3 Set MAX_TICKERS_FOR_TEST Test with a small batch first; use None when running full execution 4 Keep credentials outside source code boto3 uses the AWS CLI profile/credential chain 5 Run Python script Script calls STS to verify identity before crawling # Run local backfill. python backfill_raw_ingestion.py Full source: backfill_raw_ingestion.py import io import time from datetime import datetime, timedelta import boto3 import pandas as pd import requests import yfinance as yf from botocore.exceptions import ClientError from tqdm import tqdm # ========================================================= # AWS S3 CONFIG # ========================================================= BUCKET_NAME = &#34;stock-screener-raw-your-name&#34; RAW_ROOT = &#34;raw_us_market&#34; # boto3 retrieves credentials from the AWS CLI profile, environment variables, or IAM Role. # Do not hardcode Access Key or Secret Key in source code. # Must match the region of your bucket AWS_REGION = &#34;ap-southeast-1&#34; # ========================================================= # BACKFILL CONFIG # ========================================================= MIN_MARKET_CAP = 10_000_000_000 # 10 billion USD # Date range for price backfill BACKFILL_START_DATE = &#34;2023-01-01&#34; BACKFILL_END_DATE = (datetime.now() + timedelta(days=1)).strftime(&#34;%Y-%m-%d&#34;) # Test with 30 tickers first. Set to None to run the full S&amp;P 500 MAX_TICKERS_FOR_TEST = None # ========================================================= # AWS CLIENTS # ========================================================= # Use the default credential provider chain instead of embedding credentials in the file. session = boto3.Session(region_name=AWS_REGION) s3 = session.client(&#34;s3&#34;) sts = session.client(&#34;sts&#34;) # ========================================================= # AWS CHECK # ========================================================= def verify_aws_connection(): try: identity = sts.get_caller_identity() print(&#34;✅ AWS authentication successful&#34;) print(f&#34; Account: {identity[&#39;Account&#39;]}&#34;) print(f&#34; ARN: {identity[&#39;Arn&#39;]}&#34;) except ClientError as e: raise RuntimeError( f&#34;❌ AWS credentials error: {e.response[&#39;Error&#39;][&#39;Code&#39;]}&#34; ) from e # ========================================================= # PARQUET + S3 # ========================================================= def to_parquet_bytes(df: pd.DataFrame) -&gt; bytes: &#34;&#34;&#34; Write Parquet compatible with AWS Glue: - Avoid datetime64[ns] / TIMESTAMP(NANOS) - Date columns are saved as string YYYY-MM-DD &#34;&#34;&#34; output_df = df.copy() if not isinstance(output_df.index, pd.RangeIndex): output_df = output_df.reset_index() # Rename Date/Datetime from yfinance to price_date if &#34;Date&#34; in output_df.columns: output_df = output_df.rename(columns={&#34;Date&#34;: &#34;price_date&#34;}) if &#34;Datetime&#34; in output_df.columns: output_df = output_df.rename(columns={&#34;Datetime&#34;: &#34;price_date&#34;}) # Convert all datetime columns to string so Glue does not encounter TIMESTAMP(NANOS) for column_name in output_df.columns: if pd.api.types.is_datetime64_any_dtype(output_df[column_name]): date_series = output_df[column_name] # Remove timezone but preserve the trading date if isinstance(date_series.dtype, pd.DatetimeTZDtype): date_series = date_series.dt.tz_localize(None) # price_date / snapshot_date only need date precision if column_name in [&#34;price_date&#34;, &#34;snapshot_date&#34;]: output_df[column_name] = date_series.dt.strftime(&#34;%Y-%m-%d&#34;) else: output_df[column_name] = date_series.dt.strftime( &#34;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S&#34; ) buffer = io.BytesIO() output_df.to_parquet( buffer, index=False, compression=&#34;snappy&#34;, engine=&#34;pyarrow&#34;, version=&#34;1.0&#34; ) return buffer.getvalue() def put_df(df: pd.DataFrame, key: str): &#34;&#34;&#34;Upload a DataFrame to S3 as Parquet.&#34;&#34;&#34; if df.empty: print(f&#34;⚠️ Skipping {key}: empty DataFrame.&#34;) return try: s3.put_object( Bucket=BUCKET_NAME, Key=key, Body=to_parquet_bytes(df), ContentType=&#34;application/octet-stream&#34; ) print(f&#34;✅ Uploaded: s3://{BUCKET_NAME}/{key} | {len(df)} rows&#34;) except ClientError as e: raise RuntimeError( f&#34;❌ Cannot upload to S3.
&#34; f&#34;Error: {e.response[&#39;Error&#39;][&#39;Code&#39;]}
&#34; f&#34;Key: {key}&#34; ) from e # ========================================================= # TICKER SOURCE # ========================================================= def get_sp500_tickers(): url = &#34;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_S%26P_500_companies&#34; headers = { &#34;User-Agent&#34;: ( &#34;Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) &#34; &#34;AppleWebKit/537.36 Chrome/120.0 Safari/537.36&#34; ) } response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, timeout=30) response.raise_for_status() df_sp500 = pd.read_html(response.text)[0] # yfinance uses BRK-B instead of BRK.B return [ ticker.replace(&#34;.&#34;, &#34;-&#34;) for ticker in df_sp500[&#34;Symbol&#34;].tolist() ] # ========================================================= # COMPANY INFO (SCHEMA ERROR FIX — MISSING COLUMNS) # ========================================================= def get_company_info(ticker: str, ingestion_date: str): &#34;&#34;&#34; Company info from yfinance is current data. Schema is 100% synced with Daily Ingestion code so Spark does not report errors. &#34;&#34;&#34; stock = yf.Ticker(ticker) try: fast_info = stock.fast_info or {} market_cap = fast_info.get(&#34;marketCap&#34;, 0) except Exception: fast_info = {} market_cap = 0 if not market_cap or market_cap &lt; MIN_MARKET_CAP: return None try: info = stock.info or {} except Exception: info = {} return { &#34;ticker&#34;: ticker, &#34;snapshot_date&#34;: ingestion_date, &#34;company_name&#34;: info.get(&#34;shortName&#34;) or info.get(&#34;longName&#34;) or ticker, &#34;exchange&#34;: info.get(&#34;exchange&#34;), &#34;sector&#34;: info.get(&#34;sector&#34;), &#34;industry&#34;: info.get(&#34;industry&#34;), &#34;country&#34;: info.get(&#34;country&#34;), &#34;currency&#34;: info.get(&#34;currency&#34;), &#34;website&#34;: info.get(&#34;website&#34;), &#34;current_market_cap&#34;: market_cap or info.get(&#34;marketCap&#34;), &#34;shares_outstanding&#34;: info.get(&#34;sharesOutstanding&#34;), &#34;enterprise_value&#34;: info.get(&#34;enterpriseValue&#34;), &#34;float_shares&#34;: info.get(&#34;floatShares&#34;), &#34;beta&#34;: info.get(&#34;beta&#34;), &#34;trailing_pe&#34;: info.get(&#34;trailingPE&#34;), &#34;return_on_equity&#34;: info.get(&#34;returnOnEquity&#34;), &#34;debt_to_equity&#34;: info.get(&#34;debtToEquity&#34;), &#34;earnings_growth&#34;: info.get(&#34;earningsGrowth&#34;), &#34;revenue_growth&#34;: info.get(&#34;revenueGrowth&#34;), &#34;ingested_at&#34;: datetime.now().strftime(&#34;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S&#34;) } # ========================================================= # PRICE HISTORY (SCHEMA ERROR FIX) # ========================================================= def get_price_history(ticker: str, ingestion_date: str): &#34;&#34;&#34; Fetch price history in the range BACKFILL_START_DATE -&gt; BACKFILL_END_DATE. Schema is standardized (column names in lowercase) so Spark does not report errors. &#34;&#34;&#34; stock = yf.Ticker(ticker) df_price = stock.history( start=BACKFILL_START_DATE, end=BACKFILL_END_DATE, auto_adjust=False ) if df_price.empty: return pd.DataFrame() # Promote the Date index to a price_date column df_price = df_price.reset_index() # Process date columns if &#34;Date&#34; in df_price.columns: df_price = df_price.rename(columns={&#34;Date&#34;: &#34;price_date&#34;}) if &#34;Datetime&#34; in df_price.columns: df_price = df_price.rename(columns={&#34;Datetime&#34;: &#34;price_date&#34;}) df_price[&#34;price_date&#34;] = pd.to_datetime(df_price[&#34;price_date&#34;]).dt.tz_localize(None) # --------------------------------------------------------- # SCHEMA FIX: Rename yfinance column names -&gt; AWS Glue names # --------------------------------------------------------- rename_map = { &#34;Open&#34;: &#34;open&#34;, &#34;High&#34;: &#34;high&#34;, &#34;Low&#34;: &#34;low&#34;, &#34;Close&#34;: &#34;close&#34;, &#34;Adj Close&#34;: &#34;adj_close&#34;, &#34;Volume&#34;: &#34;volume&#34;, &#34;Dividends&#34;: &#34;dividends&#34;, &#34;Stock Splits&#34;: &#34;stock_splits&#34; } # Rename existing columns df_price = df_price.rename(columns=rename_map) # If a newer version of yfinance does not return Adj Close when auto_adjust=False if &#34;adj_close&#34; not in df_price.columns and &#34;close&#34; in df_price.columns: df_price[&#34;adj_close&#34;] = df_price[&#34;close&#34;] # Cast data types (Cast type) to float64 to avoid Integer vs Double errors in Spark numeric_columns = [&#34;open&#34;, &#34;high&#34;, &#34;low&#34;, &#34;close&#34;, &#34;adj_close&#34;, &#34;volume&#34;, &#34;dividends&#34;, &#34;stock_splits&#34;] for col in numeric_columns: if col in df_price.columns: df_price[col] = pd.to_numeric(df_price[col], errors=&#34;coerce&#34;).astype(&#34;float64&#34;) # Add metadata df_price[&#34;ticker&#34;] = ticker df_price[&#34;snapshot_date&#34;] = ingestion_date df_price[&#34;ingested_at&#34;] = datetime.now().strftime(&#34;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S&#34;) # Only keep required columns in the correct order expected_cols = [ &#34;price_date&#34;, &#34;ticker&#34;, &#34;open&#34;, &#34;high&#34;, &#34;low&#34;, &#34;close&#34;, &#34;adj_close&#34;, &#34;volume&#34;, &#34;dividends&#34;, &#34;stock_splits&#34;, &#34;snapshot_date&#34;, &#34;ingested_at&#34; ] # Filter to only columns that actually exist (avoid KeyError if yfinance is missing columns) final_cols = [c for c in expected_cols if c in df_price.columns] df_price = df_price[final_cols] return df_price # ========================================================= # BACKFILL PARTITION UPLOAD # ========================================================= def upload_prices_partitioned_by_date(df_prices: pd.DataFrame): &#34;&#34;&#34; Upload by individual trading date. Example: raw_us_market/2023/01/03/us_prices_raw.parquet raw_us_market/2023/01/04/us_prices_raw.parquet &#34;&#34;&#34; if df_prices.empty: print(&#34;⚠️ No price data to partition.&#34;) return df_prices = df_prices.copy() df_prices[&#34;price_date&#34;] = pd.to_datetime( df_prices[&#34;price_date&#34;], errors=&#34;coerce&#34; ) df_prices = df_prices.dropna(subset=[&#34;price_date&#34;]) grouped = df_prices.groupby( df_prices[&#34;price_date&#34;].dt.normalize(), sort=True ) print(f&#34;
☁️ Uploading {len(grouped)} date partitions...&#34;) for trade_date, df_one_day in tqdm( grouped, total=len(grouped), desc=&#34;Uploading date partitions&#34; ): yyyy = trade_date.strftime(&#34;%Y&#34;) mm = trade_date.strftime(&#34;%m&#34;) dd = trade_date.strftime(&#34;%d&#34;) key = ( f&#34;{RAW_ROOT}/&#34; f&#34;{yyyy}/{mm}/{dd}/&#34; f&#34;us_prices_raw.parquet&#34; ) put_df(df_one_day, key) def upload_company_info_current_snapshot( df_company_info: pd.DataFrame, ingestion_datetime: datetime ): &#34;&#34;&#34; Company info is only a current snapshot, so it is saved by the date the pipeline runs. Added float64 casting to prevent INT64 vs DOUBLE errors in Spark. &#34;&#34;&#34; if df_company_info.empty: return output_df = df_company_info.copy() # Force cast all metric columns to float64 (Double in Spark) numeric_columns = [ &#34;current_market_cap&#34;, &#34;shares_outstanding&#34;, &#34;enterprise_value&#34;, &#34;float_shares&#34;, &#34;beta&#34;, &#34;trailing_pe&#34;, &#34;return_on_equity&#34;, &#34;debt_to_equity&#34;, &#34;earnings_growth&#34;, &#34;revenue_growth&#34; ] for col in numeric_columns: if col in output_df.columns: output_df[col] = pd.to_numeric(output_df[col], errors=&#34;coerce&#34;).astype(&#34;float64&#34;) yyyy = ingestion_datetime.strftime(&#34;%Y&#34;) mm = ingestion_datetime.strftime(&#34;%m&#34;) dd = ingestion_datetime.strftime(&#34;%d&#34;) key = ( f&#34;{RAW_ROOT}/&#34; f&#34;{yyyy}/{mm}/{dd}/&#34; f&#34;us_company_info.parquet&#34; ) put_df(output_df, key) # ========================================================= # MAIN PIPELINE # ========================================================= def main(): print(&#34;=&#34; * 70) print(&#34;🚀 STOCK SCREENER - BACKFILL RAW INGESTION&#34;) print(&#34;=&#34; * 70) verify_aws_connection() run_datetime = datetime.now() ingestion_date = run_datetime.strftime(&#34;%Y-%m-%d&#34;) print(f&#34;
📅 Backfill start: {BACKFILL_START_DATE}&#34;) print(f&#34;📅 Backfill end: {BACKFILL_END_DATE}&#34;) # ----------------------------------------------------- # STEP 1: FETCH TICKERS # ----------------------------------------------------- print(&#34;
🚀 STEP 1: FETCH S&amp;P 500 TICKER LIST&#34;) all_tickers = get_sp500_tickers() if MAX_TICKERS_FOR_TEST is not None: all_tickers = all_tickers[:MAX_TICKERS_FOR_TEST] print(f&#34;✅ Tickers to process: {len(all_tickers)}&#34;) # ----------------------------------------------------- # STEP 2: FILTER BY MARKET CAP # ----------------------------------------------------- print(&#34;
🚀 STEP 2: FILTER TICKERS BY MARKET CAP&#34;) valid_tickers = [] all_company_info = [] for ticker in tqdm(all_tickers, desc=&#34;Filtering tickers&#34;): try: company_info = get_company_info( ticker=ticker, ingestion_date=ingestion_date ) if company_info is not None: valid_tickers.append(ticker) all_company_info.append(company_info) except Exception as e: print(f&#34;
⚠️ Error fetching company info for {ticker}: {e}&#34;) time.sleep(0.2) print(f&#34;
🎯 {len(valid_tickers)} tickers passed the filter.&#34;) # ----------------------------------------------------- # STEP 3: BACKFILL PRICE HISTORY # ----------------------------------------------------- print(&#34;
🚀 STEP 3: BACKFILL PRICE HISTORY&#34;) all_prices = [] for ticker in tqdm(valid_tickers, desc=&#34;Fetching price history&#34;): try: df_price = get_price_history( ticker=ticker, ingestion_date=ingestion_date ) if not df_price.empty: all_prices.append(df_price) except Exception as e: print(f&#34;
⚠️ Error fetching prices for {ticker}: {e}&#34;) time.sleep(0.2) # ----------------------------------------------------- # STEP 4: UPLOAD TO S3 # ----------------------------------------------------- print(&#34;
☁️ STEP 4: UPLOAD TO S3&#34;) if all_prices: df_prices = pd.concat(all_prices, ignore_index=True) print(f&#34;✅ Total price rows: {len(df_prices):,}&#34;) upload_prices_partitioned_by_date(df_prices) else: print(&#34;⚠️ No price data to upload.&#34;) if all_company_info: df_company_info = pd.DataFrame(all_company_info) upload_company_info_current_snapshot( df_company_info=df_company_info, ingestion_datetime=run_datetime ) else: print(&#34;⚠️ No company info to upload.&#34;) print(&#34;
🎉 BACKFILL COMPLETE!&#34;) print(f&#34;📁 Bucket: s3://{BUCKET_NAME}/{RAW_ROOT}/&#34;) if __name__ == &#34;__main__&#34;: main()

Typically, users use AWS Glue Crawler to automatically discover file structure and create tables. However, Crawlers are slow and costly. Instead, we will write a direct DDL (Data Definition Language) statement with embedded Partition Projection technique to create the table. This technique enables Athena to calculate partitions extremely fast without requiring a Crawler.
Step Action Technical Details 1 Open Query Editor In the Athena interface, switch to the Query editor tab. 2 Run DDL Copy the SQL code below, paste it into the query editor (replace the LOCATION path with your S3 Processed Bucket) and click Run. 3 Test Query Delete the old command, type a new command: SELECT * FROM dota2_matches LIMIT 10; and click Run to see the results. DDL SQL code with Partition Projection:
CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE IF NOT EXISTS dota2_matches ( `match_id` BIGINT, `account_id` BIGINT, `hero_id` INT, `is_win` BOOLEAN ) PARTITIONED BY ( `match_date` STRING ) STORED AS PARQUET LOCATION &#39;s3://dota2-processed-zone-yourname/matches_parquet/&#39; TBLPROPERTIES ( &#39;projection.enabled&#39; = &#39;true&#39;, &#39;projection.match_date.type&#39; = &#39;date&#39;, &#39;projection.match_date.range&#39; = &#39;2025-01-01,NOW&#39;, &#39;projection.match_date.format&#39; = &#39;yyyy-MM-dd&#39;, &#39;projection.match_date.interval&#39; = &#39;1&#39;, &#39;projection.match_date.interval.unit&#39; = &#39;DAYS&#39;, &#39;storage.location.template&#39; = &#39;s3://dota2-processed-zone-yourname/matches_parquet/match_date=${match_date}/&#39; );

For the Python script to push data to S3, it needs a set of keys (Access Key). We will create an IAM User and grant only the exact permissions needed to write files into the Raw Bucket.
Step Action Technical Details 1 Access IAM Find the IAM service &gt; Select Users &gt; Click Create user. 2 Enter User information User name: dota2-ingestion-bot. Skip the Provide user access to the AWS Management Console option. Click Next. 3 Initialize Policy On the Permissions screen, select Attach policies directly &gt; Click Create policy (the system will open a new tab). 4 Configure Policy (JSON) Switch to JSON format and paste the permissions code below &gt; Click Next. 5 Save Policy Policy name: S3_PutObject_Dota2_Raw. Click Create policy. 6 Attach Policy to User Return to the Create User tab, click the Refresh button, find and check S3_PutObject_Dota2_Raw &gt; Click Next &gt; Create user. 7 Generate Access Key Click into the newly created User &gt; Security credentials tab &gt; Click Create access key &gt; Select Local code. Download the .csv file containing the Access Key and Secret Key pair to your machine. JSON Policy Code (Remember to replace YOUR_BUCKET_NAME with the bucket name you created in section 1.1):
{ &#34;Version&#34;: &#34;2012-10-17&#34;, &#34;Statement&#34;: [ { &#34;Effect&#34;: &#34;Allow&#34;, &#34;Action&#34;: &#34;s3:PutObject&#34;, &#34;Resource&#34;: &#34;arn:aws:s3:::YOUR_BUCKET_NAME/*&#34; } ] }

In Chapter 2, the AWS Glue IAM Role was only granted permissions to work with S3. Now, because the Glue Job needs to write data directly to DynamoDB, you need to grant it these additional permissions.
Step Action Technical Details 1 Access IAM Role Open the IAM service &gt; Select Roles &gt; Find and click the Glue_Dota2_Processing_Role you created earlier. 2 Add Permissions In the Permissions tab, click the Add permissions button &gt; Select Create inline policy. 3 Configure JSON Switch to the JSON tab and paste the DynamoDB write permissions code below. (Remember to replace YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID with your AWS account ID). 4 Name the Policy Click Next. Set the Policy name to: DynamoDB_Write_Dota2_Metrics. 5 Complete Click Create policy to apply the new permissions to AWS Glue. JSON Inline Policy Code:
{ &#34;Version&#34;: &#34;2012-10-17&#34;, &#34;Statement&#34;: [ { &#34;Effect&#34;: &#34;Allow&#34;, &#34;Action&#34;: [ &#34;dynamodb:PutItem&#34;, &#34;dynamodb:BatchWriteItem&#34;, &#34;dynamodb:UpdateItem&#34; ], &#34;Resource&#34;: &#34;arn:aws:dynamodb:ap-southeast-1:YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID:table/dota2_hero_metrics&#34; } ] }

We will deploy the static website interface source code (HTML/JS) to a dedicated S3 Bucket configured with Static Website Hosting.
Step Action Technical Details 1 Create UI Bucket Go to S3 Console, create a new bucket named: dota2-frontend-site-yourname. 2 Disable Block Public Access Because this is a public website, under Block Public Access, UNCHECK the Block all public access box. Click Create bucket. 3 Configure Web Hosting Open the newly created Bucket &gt; Select the Properties tab &gt; Scroll down to the Static website hosting section &gt; Click Edit &gt; Select Enable. 4 Specify Default File In the Index document field, enter index.html. Click Save changes. The system provides a website endpoint URL at the bottom of this section. 5 Create Local Source On your local machine, create a file named index.html and paste the HTML/JS code block below into it. (Remember to replace the API_GATEWAY_URL variable with your Invoke URL obtained in step 5.2). 6 Upload File to S3 Return to S3 Console &gt; Objects tab &gt; Click Upload and upload the index.html file. 7 Configure Bucket Policy Switch to the Permissions tab &gt; Under Bucket policy &gt; Click Edit and paste the JSON policy below to grant public read access &gt; Click Save changes. JSON Bucket Policy Code (Remember to replace dota2-frontend-site-yourname with your bucket name):
{ &#34;Version&#34;: &#34;2012-10-17&#34;, &#34;Statement&#34;: [ { &#34;Sid&#34;: &#34;PublicReadGetObject&#34;, &#34;Effect&#34;: &#34;Allow&#34;, &#34;Principal&#34;: &#34;*&#34;, &#34;Action&#34;: &#34;s3:GetObject&#34;, &#34;Resource&#34;: &#34;arn:aws:s3:::dota2-frontend-site-yourname/*&#34; } ] }
